 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 5,
   "y": 2,
   "text": "A stone block on a wooden skid, a groove in the floor, and a plate set in front of the cheese store's door. Cheesemakers have clearly been rolling things in here for a while."
  },
  {
   "x": 18,
   "y": 3,
   "plaque": "wookey_cheddar",
   "title": "Cave-Aged Cheddar",
   "text": "CAVE-AGED CHEDDAR. Cheddar is matured in the cool, damp, steady air of Wookey Hole. The temperature hardly changes, which is just what a slow cheese wants. Cheddar the village is a few miles away, and takes the name rather seriously."
  },
  {
   "x": 13,
   "y": 4,
   "plaque": "wookey_great_chamber",
   "title": "The Great Chamber",
   "text": "CHAMBER BY CHAMBER. The show cave is a string of chambers linked by passages, with the river flowing through. Beyond the part that visitors walk, divers count more chambers that nobody can reach on foot."
  }
